Zone title fixes in engine. Use maxWidth and two-line wrapping for description. Let's implement a helper that wraps text into up to 2 lines at width. Canvas functions. Simpler:

```
const desc = t(zone.descKey);
ctx.fillText(`${range} · ${desc}`, w/2, cy+36, this.w - 28);
```
with maxWidth. The maxWidth scales horizontally instead of wrapping (might look condensed but fits). Better wrap: split words into lines max ~ this.w*0.9; draw line1 at cy+34, line2 at cy+46. But gradient only 100px tall, okay. Use font 9.5 and measureText.

Implement:
```
const desc = ...;
const maxW = this.w - 40;
const words = desc.split(' ');
let line1 = `${range} · `;
...
```
Maybe simpler: two lines:
line1 = `${range}` center at cy+36
line2 = desc truncated with ellipsis via measure loop. That gives clean zone range and description below at cy+48, still within gradient. Do that.

Also title maxWidth = w-40.

Implement with a helper to truncate.

