Better not overengineer. CSS fix is enough for wardrobe. Add a safety cap in renderHero: `const cw = Math.min(2048, ...); const ch = Math.min(2048, ...)`. But CSS renders it scaled anyway; if cap cuts size while CSS is 100%, the canvas would be stretched at lower resolution only if parent > 2048 (rare). Add cap. Also prevent dpr explosion.

